C('ArcMediaPosition','Optional shared media_session::MediaPosition object with time projections.','0x443c1dc copies a shared native position. playbackRate 0x443c300 loads native double; duration 0x443c318 divides native microseconds by 1e6, preserving signed infinity sentinels. currentTime 0x443c36c calls 0x32b5dd0 then applies the same conversion. That helper computes elapsed-time*rate, adds base position and clamps to [0,duration]; its pseudo-C return type is wrong, so source identity remains an inference. endOfMedia 0x443c3cc reads a separate flag, not currentTime==duration.','Source-backed inference: 0x32b5dd0 corresponds to MediaPosition::GetPosition/GetPositionAtTime logic at Chromium d0c02bfad08ec92a6ffcf989e53cd995e6381a4c services/media_session/public/cpp/media_position.cc:43-77; private field order in media_position.h:98-110 agrees with the metadata type and observed offsets. The header :63-67 explicitly says end_of_media may be true before duration is reached. No CEF exact timing contract is established.','Confirm time source and saturated arithmetic against bounded ARM64; test paused, negative-rate, infinite-duration and end-of-media cases.')
